Gabe | FabledMemories.com: So, yeah.

00:05:47.000 --> 00:06:02.000
Whitney Hodges: seem like they're reaching out to you like being proactive and like spotting these areas of opportunity. And I'm not sure how many calls you got on with them. But oftentimes they're like assigning a person to you on a quarterly basis. So you may meet with somebody like a few times in the course of one quarter.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:20.000
Whitney Hodges: and then you just get, like, assigned to somebody else. Like, and they do that intentionally, which is, like, really frustrating, because then you feel like you're, like, starting at square one. Um, but also, I mean, the other frustrating part is that, you know, these are their reps, they're contractors for Google, so they have.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Next.

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:23.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, Google's best interest.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:40.000
Whitney Hodges: tensions at heart. They're basically wanting to, like, get in touch with advertisers to see if you'll kind of, like, try out Google's newest features sort of things. Almost, like, it can almost be kind of a guinea pig sort of situation, right? Because Google's always rolling out new things.

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:55.000
Whitney Hodges: It's more and more sort of like AI powered as well. And yeah, oftentimes what we see is that it's just not really in the best interest of small business owners. Or you know, the Google reps don't necessarily understand.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Whitney Hodges: the business model of being a wedding pro, right? We've got a limited amount of time to be able to capture somebody while they're kind of engaged, right? And to be able to then convert them, and then it's constantly cycling a new pool of people, and these are one-time.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:15.000
Whitney Hodges: customers, right? Because ideally, they're only getting married once. Yeah.

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Hopefully. Not returning customers, yeah. Yeah.

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes, yes. Yeah, and then, you know, on the meta ad side of things.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, what we see is that, and same with Google, right, that it can be kind of overwhelming just when you're actually inside the Ads Manager account, right? It's not super intuitive as to how to set it all up, and there may be ways that Meta's, like, prompting you in terms of, like, different things to do.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:53.000
Whitney Hodges: but it's not necessarily the best suggestions, right? Like, again, it doesn't have your best interest at heart. Um, when you experimented with the meta ads, how much did you end up spending over on that side?

