00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, yeah, mm-hmm. And so you saw…

00:07:58.000 --> 00:08:15.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: No, which it was like, like overnight. And then that's when I like freaked out because it was just like, oh, here's your like invoice. And it was like 300 and something dollars. And I was like, oh no. And then I waited another month and there's like, here's another one, $400. I was like, oh no.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:31.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: I just like stopped it right away. But yeah, it is very intimidating. I joke around all the time that I could probably build a computer from scratch or a robot, but I won't be able to figure out how to do ads. It's just like.

00:08:15.000 --> 00:08:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:40.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: And then I see, I've watched so many YouTube videos, and everybody's like, oh, talking about so many different campaigns, and so many different… and I was just like, I have one…

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:59.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: And, like, one ad, no variations of it or anything. And, um, I don't know how to put the ad together, how to start to, like, get people interested. Is it too flashy? Is it too much? You know, how do you keep people's attentions nowadays? Like you said, like, you only have a tiny bit of…

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.000
Whitney Hodges: Thank you.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:17.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: So, yeah, we don't study this stuff. Like, I know people like yourself and like, you know, you dedicate this stuff. Yeah. Trends and stuff like that. My sister's trying to get into it and she tells me about how much she does like studying more about like managing people's Instagram account, not doing ads.

