Gabe | FabledMemories.com: I don't… I don't…

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:39.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: I barely use my Instagram. I think last time I posted was last year, and it's just like… I'm not a very huge Instagram… and I know that's a problem, too. I've been trying to keep my… my wife tells me all the time I need to post more and to stay relevant, but um…

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:57.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: I have a post going out today, but that's pretty much it. We got one post that I call it viral, but it's just like going by the amount of views that we get. Like it was just a lot more, but it was just one time I haven't been able to replicate it anyways.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:01.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: I'll talk forever. Yeah.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:19.000
Whitney Hodges: No, I love that. I love all the context. Yeah, and I hear you on the organic side of things, too. Like, it's a lot to keep up with, and to do the organic side well, it's like… it's this constant churn, right? It's this, like, hamster wheel of needing to post every day, or potentially multiple times a day, to actually get in front of enough of the right people.

00:10:01.000 --> 00:10:02.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Okay.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, and when we're trying to actually, like, run a business, not just market the business, right? There are only so many hours in a day, like, you have to kind of, like, pick and choose what you… what you can focus on, right? Um, and then, you know, on the flip side of things, like.

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah. Yeah.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:32.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: There.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:52.000
Whitney Hodges: the organic strategies, it's very different than the paid strategies. They can kind of complement one another, but they're definitely different things, right? And probably like you saw, you know, the virality piece of it can kind of be exciting, but at the end of the day.

00:10:44.000 --> 00:10:46.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah, yeah.

00:10:52.000 --> 00:11:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Oftentimes it doesn't really result in more business, right? Because we have no control over who are these, you know, thousands or million people that actually saw this. Are they actually people that are engaged and are getting married in the area that I serve?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:57.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: No.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:29.000
Whitney Hodges: probably not, unfortunately. So that's why we're… one of the reasons we're so passionate about teaching meta ads to wedding pros the right way, um, in a way… and when I say the right way, the way that we've seen work for countless venues and… and wedding pros. Like you said, there's so many different options.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:13.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: No.

00:11:29.000 --> 00:11:45.000
Whitney Hodges: In there, there's so many different ways that you can run campaigns, and there are people all over the internet telling you to do it one way or another. Um, but a lot of times that can be, you know, you might find a YouTube video that's for somebody who is an e-commerce business, or an online business owner.

00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:45.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:50.000
Whitney Hodges: And that, you know, again, is very different than, you know, being a wedding.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: It's hard to find. Even the stuff that I do find that there's more out there of is wedding photographers. And that's still even different from wedding video. Like you advertise differently and it's just like, so it's hard to be like, oh yeah, I just post three photos and do this. I was like, I don't have photos.

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:58.000
Whitney Hodges: Exactly.

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Whitney Hodges: And…

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, right.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:09.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Like, what do I do? So…

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:23.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, yeah, yeah. So the strategies that we teach, right, it's like in an ideal world, you're running ads on both Google and on Meta simultaneously because we find that when you're doing both, it has a compounding effect, right?

00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Like, when we think about the journey of today's buyers, or the amount of research that they're doing, like, they're looking into options for vendors, um, and researching vendors all over the place. So, they may first find you on Google, right? Go over to your website, like, take a peek, like, like what they see.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:58.000
Whitney Hodges: but they might not be ready to inquire at that point. And so that's when then retargeting on Meta specifically can be really powerful, right? Like staying in their newsfeed, like reminding them, not relying solely on the organic algorithm to do it.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:46.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Right.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:52.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Reminding them, yeah.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:12:59.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Right.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:08.000
Whitney Hodges: engineering it in a way to where somebody has visited your website. Well, we're gonna make sure that they are seeing and out of yours when they open their Facebook and their their.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:11.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Like, when we look something up on Google, and then we get 100 million ants for it, yeah.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Exactly. Yeah, yeah. So setting that up for for your business, essentially, right? And on the Meta ad side, I mean, there's a lot more that we can do than just retargeting. We also suggest conversion campaigns. So those are actual lead generation campaigns, right? Where the goal is to get somebody to fill out your inquiry form and to actually inquire with you.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, but there are also top-of-funnel client attraction campaigns that we recommend running, and what those are is they go out to completely cold audiences, so you would exclude anybody who has, uh, visited your website before, or hasn't interacted with you on social media before, and that's what helps get.

00:13:50.000 --> 00:14:07.000
Whitney Hodges: constantly like your brand in front of a fresh new pool of people, so that they can then see other ads of yours further down the funnel, right? Or click over to your Instagram and explore more, or then go over to Google and search for you. So that's kind of just an example of how it all kind of ends up.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:25.000
Whitney Hodges: working together. Um, another really important key component of it that not everybody, um, teaches, or not necessarily everybody, um, recommends doing, but we do, because we see it really kind of, uh, heavily impact and influence the lead quality.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:42.000
Whitney Hodges: is sending your ads traffic to a dedicated landing page. So I'm not sure if you tried that at all with your your Google ads, but as opposed to like sending them to the homepage of your website, which can be great, and you know it can potentially work.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:15:00.000
Whitney Hodges: But the thing about that is, when you send somebody to your website, there's a lot of different options for them, right? Like, there are different tabs for them to click around and explore. Maybe they go over to your blog, maybe they go over to your galleries. Um, it's not a true funnel, because it's giving them a ton of different options.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:19.000
Whitney Hodges: As opposed to one clear next step. And when you're paying for traffic, we want to give people one clear next step, which essentially is to inquire with you, right? To become a lead. Um, so that we do find that when you send that traffic on both the Google side and the Meta side to a long-form, dedicated landing page.

00:15:19.000 --> 00:15:37.000
Whitney Hodges: you end up with more leads, you know, a better return on your ad spend, essentially. So, inside the Ads Accelerators, that is what we teach, but also help build for you. So, I would consider it a hybrid program.

00:15:37.000 --> 00:15:53.000
Whitney Hodges: There are some things that we're doing for you. There are other things that you're responsible for, right? So the ads traffic landing page, for example, you're going to get lots of examples. You're going to get kind of our formula of what makes a great ads traffic landing page. Oftentimes it's just.

00:15:53.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Whitney Hodges: taking things from different pages of your website and turning it into one long form page, so that when people get to that page, it's kind of answering all the questions that they would have about you before inquiring right without requiring them to click around to.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:10.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: Yeah.

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:24.000
Whitney Hodges: to different places. We like that more than just sending them straight to a form, because it helps them either like self qualify or self disqualify right? They're getting to consume more information about you before they're actually taking that next step of.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Gabe | FabledMemories.com: And I've read that and I think the new layout that we have for the website does that a little bit where the homepage, it's like a mini, like a view to every section. So it has like, it has a little bit of about us, it has a little bit of the galleries, it has a little bit of the questionnaires and stuff like that and reviews.

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:25.000
Whitney Hodges: of inquiry.

00:16:30.000 --> 00:16:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Love it.

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:39.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:51.000
